<title>CHINA: CHINA'S ICBC BANK TO INCREASE LENDING IN SHANGHAI.</title>
<headline>CHINA'S ICBC BANK TO INCREASE LENDING IN SHANGHAI.</headline>
<dateline>SHANGHAI 1997-08-14</dateline>
<text>
<p>- The Shanghai branch of the Industrial and Commercial Bank of China (ICBC) plans to increase its lending by 10 billion yuan ($1.2 billion) in the second half of this year, the Xinhua News Agency said on Thursday.</p>
<p>The loans would be partly used to support 39 key state enterprises, Xinhua said.</p>
<p>The bank would also supply more loans for housing, science and technology and infrastructure, it said.</p>
<p>($1=8.3 yuan)</p>
<p>-- Shanghai Newsroom (86) 21-6279-7004</p>
